    { "id": "note-overview", "type": "note", "position": { "x": -680, "y": 0 },
      "data": { "noteKind": "text",
                "noteContent": "k-nearest neighbours has nothing to train: it keeps the training rows and labels a query by the vote of the k closest ones. ColumnSelector takes only petal length and petal width, the two columns that separate the species best, so the whole decision happens in a plane you could draw by hand. A run prints 30 predictions and then the accuracy, about 93%. Both mistakes are versicolor confused with virginica, which overlap in the real flowers too. Try n_neighbors 1, then 25.\n\nk-nearest neighbours 沒有東西要訓練：它把訓練資料留著，再用最近的 k 筆投票決定查詢點的標籤。ColumnSelector 只取花瓣長度與花瓣寬度這兩欄，因為它們最能分開三個品種，整個判斷就落在一個畫得出來的平面上。跑一次會印出 30 筆預測，再印出準確率，大約 93%。兩個錯誤都是 versicolor 與 virginica 弄混，這兩種花在真實資料裡本來就重疊。把 n_neighbors 改成 1，再改成 25 看看。",
                "noteColor": "#3d3d1a", "boundToNodeId": "start-1",
                "boundOffset": { "x": -420, "y": 0 }, "noteWidth": 360 } },
    { "id": "note-knn", "type": "note", "position": { "x": 1020, "y": -380 },
      "data": { "noteKind": "text",
                "noteContent": "weights=distance makes a nearer neighbour count for more than a far one, which is what decides the points sitting between two species. The foundations pack ships Edu-KNN: the same ports, with every distance computed in the open, so swapping it in is a one-node change.\n\nweights=distance 讓比較近的鄰居票數比較重，落在兩個品種中間的點就是這樣決定的。foundations 套件包裡有 Edu-KNN，介面相同，但把每一段距離都攤開來算給你看，換過去只要改一個節點。",
                "noteColor": "#3d3d1a", "boundToNodeId": "knn",
                "boundOffset": { "x": 0, "y": -380 }, "noteWidth": 300 } }
  ],
